-- Empowered Touch rank 1 (33879): make it do something.
--
-- The row was inert. ProcFlags 0, a single APPLY_AURA effect whose aura type is
-- SPELL_AURA_NONE, no trigger spell, no class mask. Only rank 2 (33880) carried
-- the working PROC_TRIGGER_SPELL -> Living Spores (200002), so a druid at 1/2
-- had no imbue and therefore no Living Spores DoT at all.
--
-- Worse, 2/2 did not help either. Proc diagnostics (Alonecraft.ProcDebug) over a
-- 90-second fight show aura 33880 present at exactly one timestamp -- the buff
-- burst at combat start -- and 33879 present at 224 timestamps spanning the
-- whole fight. The bot ends up carrying rank 1, which as a same-rank-chain aura
-- displaces rank 2. So the dead row was not merely unused at 1/2; it was
-- shadowing the working rank at 2/2, which is why Living Spores never landed a
-- point of damage in any measurement at either rank.
--
-- Mirrors 33880 exactly apart from ProcChance, which stays at the rank's
-- advertised 50%. The DoT itself was never the problem: 200001 is 190 per tick
-- at level 80 (BaseLevel 35, EffectRealPointsPerLevel 3.0), seven ticks over 21
-- seconds, five stacks, nature magic with a spell power coefficient.
--
-- Overrides: ProcFlags 0 -> 16384, ProcChance 101 -> 50,
-- EffectApplyAuraName1 0 -> 42, EffectTriggerSpell1 0 -> 200002,
-- EffectBasePoints1 0 -> -1, EffectDieSides1 0 -> 1,
-- EffectSpellClassMaskA1 0 -> 96, EffectSpellClassMaskA2 0 -> 33554432

DELETE FROM `alonecraft_spell_dbc` WHERE `ID` = 33879;
